# Meteofy

npm workspaces monorepo: `apps/web` (React 18 + Vite 5, JavaScript/JSX), `apps/api` (Express + TypeScript), `packages/shared` (shared TS compiled to JS + `.d.ts`). No Next.js or Tailwind.

## apps/web

- `apps/web/src/main.jsx` mounts the Redux store and `App`.
- `apps/web/src/pages` are route screens. Paths live in `apps/web/src/utils/constants/routes.js` and are registered in `apps/web/src/routes`.
- `apps/web/src/components` holds UI. A folder contains `Name.jsx` and, when styled, `Name.styles.jsx`.
- `apps/web/src/services/api` fetches weather and geocoding. Endpoint details live in `apps/web/src/utils/constants/api`.
- `apps/web/src/state` is Redux Toolkit: `cityData` for the selected city, `themeData` for dark mode.
- `apps/web/src/hooks` and `apps/web/src/utils` hold shared logic, formatters, chart config, and city lists.
- `apps/web/src/utils/styles` holds the styled-components theme and global styles.
- `apps/web/public/` holds static assets such as weather icons.

Routing is React Router 6. Styles are styled-components with the existing light and dark theme. Maps are Leaflet (Europe), SVG (Poland), and React Three Fiber (world). Charts use Chart.js. The city popup is SweetAlert2 in `apps/web/src/components/ui/modals/WeatherModal`. HTTP uses axios.

## apps/api / packages/shared

- `apps/api` — Express backend in TypeScript (object-oriented).
- `packages/shared` (`@meteofy/shared`) — shared types, schemas, constants, pure helpers. Both apps depend on it via `"@meteofy/shared": "*"`.

## Scripts (from repo root)

`npm run dev` (shared + api + web), `npm run dev:web`, `npm run dev:api`, `npm run build`, `npm run lint` (zero warnings; web + api + shared), `npm run lint:web|api|shared`, `npm run typecheck` (api + shared), `npm run format`. Workspace-scoped: `npm run <script> -w web|api|@meteofy/shared`.
